      "content": "that's a bit better, i guess. but when you say \"defending the necessity\" and \"firmly upholding its role,\" it still feels like the museum's position is the default and the repatriation stuff is just something we have to 'respect' or 'dialogue' with. \n\nif we're being totally honest, isn't the whole 'universal museum' idea just a way to justify keeping things that were taken under duress? shouldn't the statement acknowledge that some of these items can't actually be 'shared' if the people they belong to don't have them? i'm worried this still sounds like we're trying to avoid the real moral obligation of returning things.",
